/* ============================================================================
savings-goal-duration.epher -- how long different monthly deposits take
to reach a vacation fund

The finance builtin tvm_n solves the annuity equation for the term:
tvm_n(r, 0, -deposit, goal) returns the months of deposit needed to grow
an empty account to the goal at monthly rate r. Source: standard annuity
formulas; see Kellison, The Theory of Interest, chapter 3.

Sign convention: deposit negative, goal positive.

Accuracy: 12 displayed digits; the terms are fractional months.

The knobs to edit are in the knob section; everything after it is
machinery you can leave alone.
============================================================================ */

// ---- knobs ------------------------------------------------------------------
const goal = 20000          // the vacation fund target
const rate = 4%             // annual rate of return

/* ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
Rows are {monthly deposit, months to reach 20000}. Doubling the deposit
from 200 to 400 does not halve the time (86.45 to 46.32 months): the
bigger plan leans less on the account's interest. */
print("columns: monthly deposit, months to reach", goal)
for deposit in {200, 300, 400} do {deposit, tvm_n(rate / 12, 0, -deposit, goal)}
/* ---- expected output ----
= columns: monthly deposit, months to reach 20000
= {{200, 86.448382993}, {300, 60.3014883372}, {400, 46.3222365397}}
*/
